Z||000000||zebrex||03-15-2000||02:25 AM||||I ran across a recall for the 88 v6 fieros. the recall was to add a heat shield on the exhaust manifold to help prevent fires If this is still going on I would like to have my 88 formula done. If anyone knows if the recall is still active please let me know.  <A HREF="http://www.tir.com/~jaski/v6recall.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.tir.com/~jaski/v6recall.htm</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Fformula88||03-15-2000||09:35 AM||||They will still conduct the recall.  Just take your car to a Pontiac Dealer (ack).  I bought my 88 Formula in '96 and found out the recall had never been done to it.  It had 67K on it, and cannot imagine someone not having this recall done on a car they drove a lot.  Anyway, they happily did the recall.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Carrolles||03-15-2000||12:50 PM||||My understanding is that recalls do not expire.<P>Call 1(800)pmcares and give them your VIN.  Then will tell you if any recalls are still outstanding on your car.<P>I got new rear brakes and e-brake when I bought my 85se with 109000 miles on it.  I called the number and got an authorization number from GM.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Joe Trainer||03-17-2000||10:20 PM||||Called 1 (800)pmcares and was told they do not go back more than 6 years and that a call to the local Pontiac dealership would get the recall info.  Called the dealership-parts dept- and gave them the VIN# and was told all the recalls were accomplished on my car. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||fierodave||03-17-2000||11:29 PM||||If you called the dealer and they told you the recall work was done on your car  there fibbing!!!!!!(did they say the recalls were done, or that there were no open recalls?)  big difference!!!!!  <BR>They(the dealers) have no way to check by your vin number anymore!  <BR>In jan of 99 pontiac purged there computers of all fiero related material dealing in Vins. more proof  ask them for a copy of the recall work done   lol  they don't have any! <BR>so i suggest you go down there and see if they can bring it up on a screen  lol   they will say  hmmmmm  i wonder why i can't   lol<BR>all recalls on the fiero's are in affect regardless of who the owner is and the miles on the car  from the date the recall was announnced until forever!!!!!!!!!!!!  <BR>I have had three Fiero's recall work done in the last year and it took a trip there every time!  YOU HAVE TO GET THE DEALER TO AGREE TO LOOK AT THE CAR!!!<BR>within 30 seconds with there Recall manual(yep they have one) in there hand they can tell! And forget PM cares  that's a bunch of Crap  and pontiac connot make a dealer look at it either,  they can strongly suggest the dealer do it as a jesture that's it!   if you get no cooperation from your dealer tell them you would like the name and number of there district zone rep or ask if they would contact them for you  9 out 10 times  that's enough to get them to look at the car Once they agree to look at it,  your over the hump  and they will do the work  and it's free!!!!!!!!  I talk from knowing and doing  thanks for the space<BR>FD ||||reg||1
